#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan D7: linearity still CHECKS in a Saffron file.
;;
;; D7's first draft listed `^linear` as unavailable in Saffron, on the premise
;; that its guarantee needs a static type.  It does not: exactly-once is a walk
;; over the body's USES, and `any` never enters it.  Measured -- this file
;; produces the same TUR-E0101 a Turmeric file does.
;;
;; Pinned as an error fixture so a later reading of the plan's original list
;; cannot quietly turn the check off.  Its positive twin is
;; tests/fixtures/saffron-static-guarantees-still-hold.

(defn go [] (call/cc (fn [^linear k] (do (k 1) (k 2)))))

(defn main [] (println (cast (go) int)) 0)
